{
  "about": "Characters a person reading a text may not see, which text the user approves and agents then read may not hold (threat model, A3): the server refuses them (documents/agent_text.py, check_agent_text) and the browser shows each as its code point, such as [[U+202E]] (text.ts, visible). A character is hidden when it is in one of the general categories, other than the allowed controls (tab and line feed), or in a Default_Ignorable_Code_Point range (first and last, inclusive). Each case lists its hidden characters as [position in code points from 0, code point]. Unassigned code points (Cn) follow each side's Unicode version, so the cases use none that a recent version assigned.",
